<p>A US F-35 fighter jet made an emergency landing after a combat mission over Iran, after taking what US officials said appeared to be Iranian fire, according to US Central Command and multiple reports. Iran’s Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps said its air defenses struck and “seriously damaged” the aircraft over central Iran at about 2:50am local time on Thursday. It added that the jet’s fate was still under investigation and suggested it might have crashed. The US military said the aircraft landed safely and that the pilot was in stable condition, while the cause remained under investigation. If confirmed as a successful Iranian strike, the incident would be the first known case in this war of Iran hitting a US F-35, one of Washington’s most advanced and expensive combat aircraft. The episode comes amid a broader US-Israeli war with Iran that reports said began on February 28.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/1gIEoG6V7corTnx6x6h3m7EfY2HrZr2dpVc2ss7LjtGsCGOEr3xIzR8mMAObAFhgJTAbLjt-kAqVTnsoysEDUOIi0P3UU1pPA4rijYPkW1V9' alt='A F-35 jet lands on the runway of the USS Carl Vinson aircraft carrier during the Rim of the Pacific military exercises south of Oahu, Hawaii, on July 19, 2024.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Drone interceptions: The IRGC said the strike came after the interception of more than 125 US-Israeli drones, presenting the episode as evidence that Iran’s integrated air-defense network has improved.</li><li>Cost stakes: Several reports said an F-35 costs more than $100 million, underscoring the financial significance of any confirmed combat damage to the aircraft.</li><li>Missile and divert reports: The Independent said the incident involved a surface-to-air missile in Iranian airspace, while RT said US media reports indicated the jet managed to divert to a regional American airbase.</li><li>Yemen precedent: NDTV said air-defense methods based on passive infrared sensing had already shown results in Yemen when Iranian-backed Houthi forces used them.</li></ul><blockquote>The aircraft landed safely, and the pilot is in stable condition. - Captain Tim Hawkins</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps: The IRGC said its air defenses struck and seriously damaged the F-35 over central Iran, and it tied the incident to claimed improvements in Iran’s integrated air-defense systems. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1983799/irgc-claims-it-struck-us-f-35-over-central-iran-with-fighter-jets-fate-unclear'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>US Central Command: US Central Command acknowledged the emergency landing, said the pilot was stable, and said the incident was still under investigation rather than publicly confirming how the aircraft was hit. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3347217/us-f-35-hit-suspected-iranian-fire-forced-make-emergency-landing'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Unnamed US official: A US official told AFP that the aircraft appeared to have been hit by Iran, while cautioning that the investigation was still under way. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1983799/irgc-claims-it-struck-us-f-35-over-central-iran-with-fighter-jets-fate-unclear'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>NDTV analysis: NDTV argued that, if confirmed, the episode would test assumptions about stealth by showing how passive infrared tracking and aircraft heat signatures can reduce the advantage of radar evasion. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-us-war-explained-chinks-in-f-35-stealth-jet-armour-that-iran-likely-exploited-11241627#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1983799/irgc-claims-it-struck-us-f-35-over-central-iran-with-fighter-jets-fate-unclear'>IRGC claims it struck US F-35 over central Iran, with fighter jet’s fate unclear</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/us-f-35-stealth-fighter-makes-emergency-landing-after-being-hit-by-suspected-iranian-fire-reports'>US F-35